Attribution and inspiration
---------------------------

The skill-packaging format follows the open Agent Skills specification:

- Agent Skills specification - https://agentskills.io/specification.md
- Reference validator `skills-ref` - https://github.com/agentskills/agentskills
- Example skill repository - https://github.com/anthropics/skills

Two community skill repositories were read as structural examples during design
(layout of SKILL.md plus supporting agents/ references/ scripts/ folders, and the
Chinese-language skill development guide). They are references only; no source code,
text or assets are copied from them:

- https://github.com/nextlevelbuilder/ui-ux-pro-max-skill
- https://github.com/sanshao85/claude-skills-guide

MCP server definitions are consumed through the local MCP client configuration of the
host agent (Claude Code, Codex, Qoder, GitHub Copilot). This project does not bundle
or redistribute any MCP server implementation.

No third-party code is vendored in this repository. The runtime uses only the Python
standard library; PyYAML and jsonschema are optional extras.
